  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: JxPath\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: JxPath\n       Program: commons-jxpath\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JxPath/JxPath.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-jxpath.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JxPath/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 22\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: JxPath-1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nfab38abb27f2f92b9340cfc232eb5517434bf138\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2007-01-10 18:27:20 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nJXPATH-12\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/JXPATH-12\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMModelTest::testGetNode\n   --> java.lang.NullPointerException\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMModelTest::testGetNode\n   --> java.lang.NullPointerException\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMNodePointer\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Descendant or self axis does not work correctly at root node\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Resolved | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nGiven the following XML document: <root id=\"1234\"/>\nand the XPath: //root/@id/text().\n\nJXPath returns null instead of \"1234\".\n\nJXPathContext context = JXPathContext.newContext(doc);\nassertEquals(value, context.selectSingleNode(\"//root/@id/text()\"));\n\nThe attached JUnit test highlights the problem. It seems that JXPath does not\nfind the root node if it is accessed with the axis descendant-or-self.\n\nComments:\n\n[Simon Raess]: Created an attachment (id=17625)\nUnit test reproducing the described bug\n\n[Simon Raess]: Note, I reproduced that bug using the JDOM model. I have not checked whether it\nworks in other models.\n\n[J\u00f6rg Heinicke]: Just wondering: Does an attribute have a text child node (from a pure XML POV)?\n\nIf yes, from a JXPath POV: Might @id/text() be the problem and not the root node?\n\n[Simon Raess]: Actually, if I'm correct: @id/text() does not make sense from the XML POV. But, the issues is not related to \nthat particular XPath. It is sufficient to use //root to reproduce the problem. I'm quite confident that the \nproblem is caused by a bug in JXPath (i.e. incorrect handling of // at the root of the document.\n\n[Marcin Sarniak]: Adding a patch proposition for this bug (patch.jxpath-12.txt). \n\nAs written here before, bug actually appears when xpatch is like \"//root\".\nIt appears also when a dom is inside any java structure \nFor example: map.put(\"test\", new Document(new Element(\"root\"))); xpatch for\n\"//root\" would return null.\n\nExactly the same bug was both for JDom and Dom; both are fixed.\n\nModifies 4 files:\n main:\n   JDOMNodePointer.java\n   DOMNodePointer.java\n tests:  \n   JDOMModelTest.java\n   DOMModelTest.java\n\nThis patch is to latest version (2.2?), not to version 1.2, reported as affected here.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer (fixed)\n@@ -113,7 +113,8 @@\n             int nodeType = node.getNodeType();\n             switch (((NodeTypeTest) test).getNodeType()) {\n                 case Compiler.NODE_TYPE_NODE :\n-                    return nodeType == Node.ELEMENT_NODE;\n+                    return nodeType == Node.ELEMENT_NODE\n+                            || nodeType == Node.DOCUMENT_NODE;\n                 case Compiler.NODE_TYPE_TEXT :\n                     return nodeType == Node.CDATA_SECTION_NODE\n                         || nodeType == Node.TEXT_NODE;\n\n--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMNodePointer (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMNodePointer (fixed)\n@@ -373,7 +373,7 @@\n         else if (test instanceof NodeTypeTest) {\n             switch (((NodeTypeTest) test).getNodeType()) {\n                 case Compiler.NODE_TYPE_NODE :\n-                    return node instanceof Element;\n+                    return (node instanceof Element) || (node instanceof Document);\n                 case Compiler.NODE_TYPE_TEXT :\n                     return (node instanceof Text) || (node instanceof CDATA);\n                 case Compiler.NODE_TYPE_COMMENT :"
